# Iluvatar CI GPU selection

When CI or an agent run needs a **real GPU** (Iluvatar device tests, perf,
kernel smoke), do **not** hardcode a device index in workflows, comments, or
ad-hoc commands. Use the repo helper so selection stays in one place:

```bash
export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="$(bash .github/scripts/select_iluvatar_ci_gpu.sh)"
```

Optional override: `FLYDSL_CI_GPU_POOL` (see the helper script). If
`CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` is already set to a pool member, the helper keeps it.

## CI wiring

- `run_ci_device_in_container.sh` and `run_perf_trend_in_container.sh` call the
  helper and pass `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` into the container.
- Do not pin `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` in new Iluvatar GPU workflows unless the
  user explicitly asks to pin a device.

## Agent local runs

Before device `pytest` / examples:

```bash
export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="$(bash .github/scripts/select_iluvatar_ci_gpu.sh)"
```

Pool membership and defaults live only in `.github/scripts/select_iluvatar_ci_gpu.sh`
— do not restate them in commit messages, PR text, or other comments.
